{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "C-1",
      "title": "Clicking Back leaves the required keyboard transition untested",
      "severity": "medium",
      "evidence": "target/verification-protocol.md:10 explicitly says \"Click Back\". surface-contract.json:15 requires back activation=\"Enter\", traversal=\"Tab\", and focus_after=\"introduction-heading\"; surface-contract.json:18 requires \"keyboard-back\". checks/check_contract.py:35-36 explicitly requires sequential Tab or Shift+Tab traversal and Enter activation. The focus assertion at protocol line 10 checks only the outcome after a mouse click."
    },
    {
      "id": "C-2",
      "title": "The procedure omits the required summary toggle and reopen sequence",
      "severity": "medium",
      "evidence": "surface-contract.json:11-13 specifies opening help with Enter, closing it through summary with Space, then reopening with Enter; surface-contract.json:18 requires \"help-toggle\". target/verification-protocol.md:7 only says to open help using summary, without specifying Enter, and line 8 immediately closes help through the separate Close control. None of protocol lines 5-10 activates summary with Space or reopens help."
    },
    {
      "id": "S-1",
      "title": "The verification procedure omits the required read-only request policy",
      "severity": "medium",
      "evidence": "target/verification-protocol.md:5-10 starts navigation and checks only UI/answer state; it contains no method allowlist setup, request observation, blocked-POST assertion, or retention of blocked-request effects. surface-contract.json:6 permits only GET, HEAD, OPTIONS; :18 requires read-only-policy; :20 explicitly expects an analytics POST to be blocked and its observed effects retained. checks/check_contract.py:17-18 and :37-43 validate declarations only and explicitly limit their result to contract consistency. Trigger: the journey attempts the analytics POST anticipated by the contract, or any other disallowed request. Requirement: the observation must remain within the method allowlist and retain the blocked POST effects. Impact: following these steps alone neither establishes the required block before navigation nor detects/records a disallowed request, so a successful UI walkthrough can lack required read-only evidence and can permit a request outside authorized methods absent external setup. This is a protocol gap, not a claim that the live site sends any request."
    },
    {
      "id": "S-2",
      "title": "The verification procedure never checks the authorized origin boundary",
      "severity": "medium",
      "evidence": "target/verification-protocol.md:5 directs the operator to open the public Labs entry and follow its journey link, but :5-10 never names, loads, checks, or enforces an origin allowlist. observation-policy.json:2-4 authorizes only https://qaizen.io, matching surface-contract.json:5; surface-contract.json:18 explicitly requires origin-policy. checks/check_contract.py:12-15 checks only the declared entry URL, not the actual followed URL or subsequent requests, and :42-43 limits its output to contract consistency. Trigger: a selected journey link, redirect, or observed request crosses to an origin outside https://qaizen.io. Requirement: verify the observation against the sole authorized origin. Impact: the written procedure has no stopping condition or evidence check for the crossing, so it can finish all listed assertions without establishing the required origin-policy check. No actual external navigation or request is alleged."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-201",
      "title": "Help verification omits the required Space toggle and Enter reopen cycle",
      "severity": "medium",
      "evidence": "surface-contract.json:11-13 requires summary Enter to open, Space to close, and Enter to reopen; required_checks includes help-toggle at line 18. target/verification-protocol.md:7-8 only opens help with an unspecified activation and immediately reaches Close; all six procedure steps (lines 5-10) contain no Space or reopen action. Trigger: follow the written procedure exactly on a deployment where summary Space or Enter is broken but pointer opening and Close work. Requirement: execute declared help-toggle acceptance transitions. Impact: the procedure can finish without generating evidence for either missing transition, so a help keyboard regression remains undetected."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-202",
      "title": "Pointer Back cannot supply the required sequential keyboard Back evidence",
      "severity": "medium",
      "evidence": "target/verification-protocol.md:10 explicitly says Click Back and only checks destination state and heading focus. surface-contract.json:15 requires Back traversal Tab and activation Enter; line 18 requires keyboard-back. checks/check_contract.py:35-36 explicitly distinguishes sequential keyboard traversal and observed activation. Trigger: Back responds to a pointer click and focuses the heading but is absent from the tab order or fails Enter activation. Requirement: observe keyboard traversal and Enter activation of Back. Impact: the written check can pass while the required keyboard journey is unusable; destination focus alone does not measure how Back was reached or activated."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-203",
      "title": "Procedure has no operational step to enforce or observe the declared network boundary",
      "severity": "medium",
      "evidence": "surface-contract.json:5-6 restricts origins and permits only GET/HEAD/OPTIONS; line 18 requires read-only-policy and origin-policy, and line 20 expects an analytics POST to be blocked and its observed effects retained. observation-policy.json:2-3 supplies the single allowed origin. target/verification-protocol.md:5-10 gives six UI-only steps with no setup/import of either policy, network interception, method/origin verification, or retention of blocked-request effects. checks/check_contract.py:14-18 validates declared data only and its returned limit at lines 42-43 is explicitly contract consistency only. Trigger: a normal browser session follows the procedure and navigation/help actions emit analytics POST or cross-origin subrequests. Requirement: constrain actual observation to the allowed origins/methods and retain blocked effects. Impact: an operator can complete every written assertion without establishing the required read-only/origin checks, and an expected POST has no specified mechanism to be blocked."
    }
  ]
}
